# Glossary Rules

Canonical terminology reference: `docs/BẢNG QUY TẮC Chat GPT tongHop.md`

## File: `web/data/glossary/terms.yaml`

Each entry maps Chinese (`zh`) to **two renderings**:

```yaml
series: default  # or series name
terms:
  - zh: "般若"
    hv: "Bát nhã"
    vi: "Bát nhã"
    notes: "Prajna; not 'trí tuệ' alone when technical"
    sanskrit: "prajñā"
  - zh: "菩薩摩訶薩"
    hv: "Đại Bồ tát"
    vi: "Đại Bồ tát"
    compound: true
    notes: "Semantic compound; overrides word-by-word in .hv.md"
  - zh: "比丘"
    hv: "Tỳ kheo"
    vi: "Tỳ kheo"
    alt_vi: ["nam cư sĩ"]
```

## Fields

| Field | Layer | Use |
|-------|-------|-----|
| `zh` | lookup | Primary key; use full compound when fixed |
| `hv` | `.hv.md` | Hán-Việt — word-by-word or compound per entry |
| `vi` | `.vi.md` | Readable Vietnamese; prefer established Hán Việt |
| `sanskrit` / `pali` | notes | International diacritic form (e.g. prajñā) |
| `doctrine: true` | both | Requires reviewer sign-off |
| `compound: true` | both | Single-unit render; overrides character-by-character in `.hv.md` |
| `alt_vi` | vi | Forbidden synonyms — never use in translation |
| `status: pending` | — | Block translation until resolved |

## Term categories (curator / build-glossary)

| Category | Policy | Examples |
|----------|--------|----------|
| Phật hiệu | Capitalize | Phật, Như Lai, Thế Tôn, Chánh Biến Tri |
| Bồ tát | Hán Việt; never Giác hữu tình | Bồ tát, Đại Bồ tát, Quán Thế Âm |
| Thanh văn | Hán Việt | Xá Lợi Phất, A Nan, Ca Diếp |
| Tăng đoàn | Fixed forms; `alt_vi` for cư sĩ | Tỳ kheo, Sa di, Ưu bà tắc |
| Quả vị | Hán Việt | Tu đà hoàn, A la hán |
| Pháp tu / giáo lý | Hán Việt | Bát nhã ba la mật, duyên khởi, không |
| Địa danh | Title Case per syllable; no hyphens | Xá Vệ, Kỳ Viên |
| Chức danh | Lowercase generic + capitalize name | Tam tạng pháp sư Huyền Trang |
| Tên kinh | `{Name} Kinh` not `Kinh {Name}` | Kim Cương Kinh |

## Principles

- **One `zh` → one `hv` and one `vi`** per series scope
- When `hv` and `vi` are the same (proper names, established compounds), set both explicitly
- When layers differ: `hv` stays âm dịch; `vi` uses natural thuần Việt only when needed (e.g. 修多羅 hv `Tu Đa La`, vi `kinh`)
- No hyphens in `hv` or `vi`; capitalization per terminology doc
- `alt_vi`: register forbidden forms (e.g. `nam cư sĩ` for 比丘, `Giác hữu tình` for 菩薩)
- Legacy entries with only `vi` are treated as `hv` until curated

## First occurrence (`.vi.md` only)

- Optional inline parenthetical: `Bát nhã (般若)` on first use of hard terms
- Agents do **not** add by default; user may request or add via web **Insert footnote**
- Footnotes: `[^n]` inline + definitions after `<!-- footnotes -->`; body line count unchanged

## Translation usage

| Output | Use field | Agent / skill |
|--------|-----------|---------------|
| `.hv.md` | `hv` | `/sino-vietnamese-translator`, translate-sino-vietnamese |
| `.vi.md` | `vi` | `/translator`, translate-buddhist-text |

Never substitute `hv` readings in `.vi.md` or `vi` readings in `.hv.md` unless the two fields are identical in the glossary.

## Updates

- New term: add `hv` + `vi` before first use in translation
- Conflict between series: use `series:` scoped files (`web/data/glossary/{series}.yaml`)
- Auto-extract from HV drafts populates `hv`; curator must set `vi` when it differs
